#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:9
msgid "Learning about topics - tutorial"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:11
msgid ""
"Topics are one of the main communication types used for moving data around a "
"ROS system. This article walks you through using ``rqt_graph`` and other "
"command-line tools to examine how nodes connect over topics. A hands-on "
"exercise with Turtlesim helps you understand how data moves around the ROS "
"graph."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:15
msgid "**Area: Framework | Content-type: tutorial | Experience: beginner**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:19
msgid "Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:22
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:24
msgid ""
"Nodes publish information to topics, which allows any number of other nodes "
"to subscribe to and access that information. You can use ``rqt_graph`` and "
"command-line tools to introspect and examine the connections between nodes "
"that share topics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:28
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:30
msgid ""
":doc:`Install ROS <../../../../Get-Started/Installation>` and :doc:`set up "
"your workspace <../../../../Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:31
msgid "Make sure you understand:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:33
msgid ""
"The function of :doc:`nodes <../../../nodes/Working-with-nodes/Understanding-"
"ROS2-Nodes/Understanding-ROS2-Nodes>` and how to work with them"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:34
msgid ""
"The different :doc:`interface types <../../../Interfaces-Topics-Services-"
"Actions>`, including topics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:37
msgid "Steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:40
msgid ""
"Remember to source ROS in every new terminal you open. See :doc:`Configuring "
"environment <../../../../Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:44
msgid "1 Run turtlesim nodes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:46
msgid "Open a new terminal and run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:48
msgid "$ ros2 run turtlesim turtlesim_node"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:52
msgid "Open another terminal and run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:54
msgid "$ ros2 run turtlesim turtle_teleop_key"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:58
msgid ""
"Names of these nodes are ``/turtlesim`` and ``/teleop_turtle`` by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:63
msgid "2 Visualize the nodes with rqt_graph"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:65
msgid ""
"Throughout this tutorial, you use ``rqt_graph`` to visualize the changing "
"nodes and topics, as well as the connections between them. ``rqt_graph`` is "
"a graphical introspection tool whose highlighting feature is helpful when "
"you examine more complex systems with multiple nodes and topics connected in "
"many different ways."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:68
msgid ""
":doc:`Using turtlesim, ros2, and rqt <../../../../Get-Started/Introducing-"
"Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim>` tells you how to install ``rqt`` and all "
"its plugins, including ``rqt_graph``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:70
msgid "To run ``rqt_graph``, open a new terminal and enter the command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:72
msgid "$ ros2 run rqt_graph rqt_graph"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:76
msgid ""
"You can also open ``rqt_graph`` by opening ``rqt`` and selecting **Plugins** "
"> **Introspection** > **Node Graph**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:78
msgid "You should see a graph similar to this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:83
msgid ""
"If your graph looks different, change the first drop-down to **Nodes/Topics "
"(active)** and click the refresh button to its left."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:85
msgid ""
"In the graph, you should see the ``/turtlesim`` and ``/teleop_turtle`` nodes "
"and the topic connecting them, as well as two actions around the periphery. "
"If you hover your mouse over the topic in the center, you should see the "
"colour highlighting shown in the screenshot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:88
msgid ""
"The graph illustrates how the ``/turtlesim`` node and the ``/teleop_turtle`` "
"node communicate with each other over a topic. The ``/teleop_turtle`` node "
"publishes data (the keystrokes you enter to move the turtle around) to the "
"``/turtle1/cmd_vel`` topic, and the ``/turtlesim`` node is subscribed to "
"that topic to receive the data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:93
msgid "3 List the active topics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:95
msgid ""
"In a new terminal, run the ``ros2 topic list`` command to list of all the "
"topics currently active in the system:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:97
msgid "$ ros2 topic list"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:101
#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:118
#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:193
#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:589
msgid "The terminal returns:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:103
msgid ""
"/parameter_events\n"
"/rosout\n"
"/turtle1/cmd_vel\n"
"/turtle1/color_sensor\n"
"/turtle1/pose"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:112
msgid ""
"Now run ``ros2 topic list -t`` to get the same list, but with the topic type "
"appended in brackets:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:114
msgid "$ ros2 topic list -t"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:120
msgid ""
"/parameter_events [rcl_interfaces/msg/ParameterEvent]\n"
"/rosout [rcl_interfaces/msg/Log]\n"
"/turtle1/cmd_vel [geometry_msgs/msg/Twist]\n"
"/turtle1/color_sensor [turtlesim_msgs/msg/Color]\n"
"/turtle1/pose [turtlesim_msgs/msg/Pose]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:128
msgid ""
"These attributes, particularly the type, are how nodes confirm they are "
"exchanging compatible data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:130
msgid ""
"To show all of the topics in the ``rqt_graph``, you can clear all of the "
"**Hide** checkboxes. For now, leave those options checked to avoid confusion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:137
msgid "4 View the data being published to a topic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:139
msgid "To see the data being published on a topic, use:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:141
msgid "$ ros2 topic echo <topic_name>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:145
msgid ""
"In a previous step, you learned that ``/teleop_turtle`` publishes data to ``/"
"turtlesim`` over the ``/turtle1/cmd_vel`` topic. Use ``echo`` to introspect "
"that topic:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:148
msgid "$ ros2 topic echo /turtle1/cmd_vel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:152
msgid ""
"At first, this command won't return any data. That's because it's waiting "
"for ``/teleop_turtle`` to publish something."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:155
msgid ""
"Return to the terminal where ``turtle_teleop_key`` is running and use the "
"arrow keys to move the turtle around."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:158
msgid ""
"The ``turtle_teleop_key`` terminal must be the active window to capture your "
"key presses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:160
msgid ""
"You should see position data being published for every movement that you "
"make:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:162
#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:306
msgid ""
"linear:\n"
"  x: 2.0\n"
"  y: 0.0\n"
"  z: 0.0\n"
"angular:\n"
"  x: 0.0\n"
"  y: 0.0\n"
"  z: 0.0\n"
"  ---"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:174
msgid ""
"Now return to ``rqt_graph``, uncheck the **Debug** box, and select the "
"**Refresh** button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:178
msgid ""
"The node created by the ``echo`` command should appear. In this example it "
"is ``/_ros2cli_26646``, but the number on your machine will be different. "
"You can now see that the publisher is publishing data on the ``cmd_vel`` "
"topic, and two subscribers are subscribed to it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:183
msgid "5 View the publisher and subscriber counts for a topic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:185
msgid ""
"Any number of nodes can publish on a topic, and any number of nodes can "
"subscribe to that topic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:187
msgid "To see the publisher and subscriber counts for a topic, run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:189
msgid "$ ros2 topic info /turtle1/cmd_vel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:195
msgid ""
"Type: geometry_msgs/msg/Twist\n"
"Publisher count: 1\n"
"Subscription count: 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:202
msgid "5.1 View detailed topic information"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:204
msgid ""
"To get more detailed information about a topic, use the ``--verbose`` (or ``-"
"v``) flag:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:206
msgid "$ ros2 topic info /turtle1/cmd_vel --verbose"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:210
msgid "This will return additional details, including:"
