#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:611
msgid "FAQs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:613
msgid "Why does ``ros2 topic echo`` show no data when I first run it?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:614
msgid ""
"That is expected if nothing is publishing on the topic yet. The ``echo`` "
"command waits for a publisher to send a message. Start or use a publisher "
"(for example ``turtle_teleop_key``) and move the turtle to see data appear."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:618
msgid ""
"What is the difference between ``ros2 topic list`` and ``ros2 topic list -"
"t``?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:619
msgid ""
"``ros2 topic list`` returns the names of all active topics. Adding ``-t`` "
"appends each topic's message type in brackets, which shows what type of data "
"travels on each topic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:622
msgid "Can a topic have more than one publisher or subscriber?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:623
msgid ""
"Yes. Multiple nodes can publish on the same topic, and multiple nodes can "
"subscribe to it at the same time. Use ``ros2 topic info`` to see how many "
"publishers and subscribers are connected to a topic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:627
msgid "Why must publishers and subscribers use the same message type?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:628
msgid ""
"Both sides must agree on the message structure so data can be serialized and "
"interpreted correctly. Check a topic's type with ``ros2 topic list -t`` or "
"``ros2 topic info``, then inspect the type with ``ros2 interface show``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:631
msgid "Why does ``ros2 topic pub`` auto-complete not work on Windows?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics.rst:632
msgid ""
"The auto-complete options for publishing (dictionary auto-complete and the "
"raw auto-completed string) rely on shell behaviour that is not supported on "
"Windows. On Windows, type message data manually as YAML strings instead of "
"using tab completion for the message field template."
msgstr ""
